 "result": "I wrote the Dockerfile and two supporting files. I couldn't build or run anything here, so none of it has been tested.\n\n- **`Dockerfile`**: a three-stage build.\n  - The first stage builds the web app (`web/`, via `npm ci` and `npm run build`, with `docs/` available because the in-app guide is generated from it).\n  - The second stage compiles the Go program (`./cmd/app`) with that web app embedded. It uses `CGO_ENABLED=0` and takes the version from `VERSION`. Optional build args `VERSION`, `TMDB_API_KEY`, `OPENSUBTITLES_API_KEY`, `TRAKT_CLIENT_ID` and `SIMKL_CLIENT_ID` are stamped in. The stage is named `build` and outputs `/out/app`, which is what `tools/push-update.sh` expects.\n  - The last stage is Alpine with `par2cmdline`, `p7zip`, `su-exec`, `ca-certificates` and `tzdata`, matching `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`. It exposes 8264 (web) and 58264 (torrent peers, TCP and UDP), declares `/config` as a volume, and has a healthcheck on `/api/version`.\n- **`docker-entrypoint.sh`**: a small start script that does the following.\n  - It applies `TZ` and creates the config folder.\n  - It creates the default downloads, movies and TV folders if they are missing.\n  - It drops to `PUID:PGID` (default 1000:1000) with `su-exec`. If the container is started with a non-root user, it runs the program directly.\n- **`.dockerignore`**: leaves out `.git`, `node_modules`, local `web/dist`, local data folders, `.env` and database files.\n\n- **`docker/entrypoint.sh` not created:** `internal/selfupdate/entrypoint_test.go` expects a `docker/entrypoint.sh` that doesn't exist in this tree. It would handle installed updates and boot-loop protection. I didn't create that path, because those tests assert detailed behaviour I couldn't reproduce. My entrypoint is a plain `/opt/mediarium/app` start with no installed-update logic, so the in-app \"Update now\" flow won't be able to swap in new binaries.\n- **Base images assumed:** I assumed `golang:1.26-alpine` (`go.mod` needs 1.26.11 or later), `node:24-alpine` and `alpine:3.22` exist.",
